{
    name: "Atlas (Historical Borders)",
    open: false,
    category_type: "discrete",
    "simplified_borders": {
        name: "Simplified Borders",
        description: [
            "### Simplified Borders",
            "Simplified de facto borders used for statistical purposes. Shapes after 1886AD are not coloured.",
            "<details>",
            "<summary>Methodology</summary>",
            "Joint database between Atlas 0.6b and [C-Shapes 2.0](https://icr.ethz.ch/data/cshapes/CShapes-2.0_Codebook.pdf).",
            "",
            "Atlas 0.6b was heavily inspired by Cliopatria, but differed in containing border adjustments to align better with historical reality. Both [Cliopatria](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-04516-9) and C-Shapes 2.0 are known to contain encoding and historical errors, but allow for qualitative encoding from academic databases, i.e. via [Seshat](https://seshat-db.com/).",
            "</details>"
        ],
        filepaths: [
            {
                path: "${l_atlas}/CShapes-2.0.geojson",
                type: "vector.geojson",
                domain: [
                    1886,
                    2026
                ]
            },
            {
                path: "${l_atlas}/atlas.naissance",
                type: "vector.naissance",
                domain: [
                    -3500,
                    1886
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    "detailed_borders": {
        name: "Detailed Borders",
        description: [
            "### Detailed Borders",
            "De facto territorial frontiers from 3500BC to 2025AD. This dataset is chunked, meaning countries may have keyframes beyond the time period currently being viewed.",
            "<details>",
            "<summary>Methodology</summary>",
            "Largely based on presence modelling (convex hull) over a borderpool. This means there is a lot of work in terms of manually refining and iterating over the current data at hand, as many borders during conflict periods are poor interpolations which require fixing.",
            "",
            "In addition, regions outside of Europe, India, and Africa tend to be overly simplified (i.e. Warlord Era, Native American polities). We intend on improving these weakpoints and adding diplomatic relations prior to a full release.",
            "</details>"
        ],
        filepaths: [
            {
                path: "${l_df}/0.476.1.1.naissance",
                type: "vector.naissance",
                domain: [
                    -3500,
                    476
                ]
            },
